from pathlib import Path
p=Path('docs/mechanical/fusion-controller/ASSEMBLY-AND-PRINT-GUIDE.md');s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('three P08 cam alternatives.','three P08 cam alternatives and two P18 coupling-disc fits (27 print files total; print one of each alternative).')
s=s.replace('It avoids gears and backlash.','It eliminates the gear mesh, but printed coupling clearances can still produce reversal play. The rotor has a radial M3 clamp onto the shaft flat. The default Oldham grooves are 4.2 mm for 4 mm tongues; an optional 4.1 mm disc is provided. Choose the closest fit that slides freely after cleanup, never a binding fit. Measure sensor readings when approaching every gate from both directions before final calibration.')
s=s.replace('CNC Kitchen M3 × 5.7 mm heat-set insert | 15','CNC Kitchen M3 × 5.7 mm heat-set insert | 16').replace('3 rotor,','4 rotor,')
s=s.replace('M3 × 16 | 3 | Coupling clamps','M3 × 16 | 4 | Three coupling clamps and rotor-to-shaft clamp')
s=s.replace('M3 × 30 | 2 | Spring cup guides','M3 × 35 | 2 | Spring cup guides')
s=s.replace('M3 washers, approx. OD7 × 0.5 | 7 | Coupling 3, carriage 2, guides 2','M3 washers, approx. OD7 × 0.5 | 8 | Coupling 3, carriage 2, guides 2, rotor clamp 1')
s=s.replace('M4 × 25 + M4 nut | 1 each | Spring preload','M4 × 25 socket head Ø7 + M4 nut | 1 each | Spring preload; keep the head within the modeled envelope')
s=s.replace('M5 × 25 | 6 | Four rail mounts and two stop cores','M5 × 25 | 2 | Stop cores |\n| M5 × 30 | 4 | Rail mounts with the specified 5 mm total metal spacer stack')
s=s.replace('M5 washers, approx. OD10 × 1 | 4 | Rail mounting','M5 metal spacers, OD10 / ID5.4 × 5 mm | 4 | Rail mounting; a measured washer stack totaling 5 mm may substitute')
s=s.replace('all 15','all 16').replace('M3 × 30 bolts','M3 × 35 bolts').replace('using M5 × 25 and T-nuts','using M5 × 30, the 5 mm metal spacer stacks and T-nuts')
s=s.replace('Do not tighten the cap to remove designed clearance.','Do not tighten the cap to remove designed clearance. Snug the radial rotor screw against the shaft D-flat; use a flat-ended screw and do not crush the printed shaft. Its purpose is transmitting low sensor torque without rattling through socket clearance.')
s=s.replace('The right-side service opening is intended to let the cam slide sideways out after removing these screws. The head recesses and axial path must remain unobstructed.','For replacement, remove its screws, back off/remove the M4 adjuster and hold the follower about 5 degrees down (roughly 3 mm at the roller) with a suitable temporary holding tool, then slide the cam 40 mm sideways through the right-side opening. The outer cheek otherwise catches the cam. Removing the adjuster does NOT unload the spring: its cup can only rise about 1 mm. The calculated holding force is roughly 27 N with the candidate spring. For unloaded servicing instead, restrain the cup, release the guide hardware carefully and remove the spring before moving the cam. Do not let the spring eject.')
s=s.replace('Check actual bolt reach in your slots before tightening.','The exact frame mesh has a web 6.2 mm behind the slot face. The modeled M5 × 30 with 5 mm total metal spacer stack penetrates 5 mm, leaving 1.2 mm nominal web clearance. Do not add a further washer beyond that 5 mm total. Check the selected T-nut provides at least 3 mm of full effective thread engagement (or its supplier\'s greater requirement) without bottoming before tightening.')
s=s.replace('spring cup print top face down','spring cup print top face down')
s=s.replace('Nominal spring space is 17 mm; follower motion and the permitted extra preload reduce it to about 15.2 mm.','Nominal spring space is 17 mm; follower motion and the permitted extra preload reduce it to about 15.2 mm. With the adjuster backed off and follower depressed 5 degrees for servicing, the spring space is about 16.3 mm. The preload-limit collar is 2 mm tall in the final design.')
s += '\n## Fusion inspection\n\nThe native file includes three revolute joints (lever, follower and free roller) and rigid groups. The main lever has +/-52 degree limits. The follower includes service travel down to -6 degrees. These are inspection joints: they do not automatically solve cam contact, spring deformation or Oldham misalignment. The 7-gate cam is visible by default; alternative cams and the tight coupling disc are hidden. Do not enable overlapping alternatives together.\n\nSlicer validation used normal supports on the listed supported parts. The supplied deliverable contains geometry, not printer G-code: re-slice in Bambu Studio using your installed P2S profile and inspect support access. CLI validation generated layers for all meshes but reported vendor preset metadata/tool-command warnings, so its printer files are not released.\n'
p.write_text(s)
